.SH NAME
perturb \- Set the expression value of a set of genes to the given values, i.e. run a
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIperturb(\fBtree\fR as <generic> XGBoostGRN, 
\fBgenes\fR as any, 
\fBexpression\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Set the expression value of a set of genes to the given values, i.e. run a
 \fBCustom\fR mode in silico intervention.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBtree\fB \fR\- the trained [XGBoostGRN](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GeneTree.XGBoostGRN) model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- a character vector of the target gene id.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBexpression\fB \fR\- 
 a numeric vector of the expected expression value of each target gene, in the
 same order as **genes**; the genes are set to these values and
 are clamped during the whole iteration.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the [InterventionResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.BioSystem.Intervention.InterventionResult) object of the intervention, which could be
 exported via the \fBmake_exports\fR api of the \fBbnlearn\fR package module;
 an R# error message object is returned when the sizes of the two vectors do not
 match or the prediction fails.
.PP
